        "text": "This is a photo of a grocery/household store receipt. Extract every line item you can read. Respond with ONLY a JSON object, no prose, no markdown fences: {\"store\": string, \"date\": string (YYYY-MM-DD, your best reading of the receipt date), \"items\": [{\"item\": string (product name as printed, cleaned up if obviously abbreviated), \"price\": number (this line's actual paid price), \"category\": string (one of: Produce, Dairy, Meat, Prepared, Seafood, Pantry, Frozen, Beverages, Snacks, Household), \"size\": string|null (pack size/weight ONLY if actually printed on the receipt — do not guess or estimate one), \"unit_label\": string|null (e.g. \"$/lb\", \"$/ct\" — only if size is non-null and a unit price is derivable)}]}. If any field for an item is genuinely unreadable or absent from the receipt, use null for that field rather than guessing — per this project's convention, an uncertain value must never be silently invented."
      }
    ]
  }]
} }}

